  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ goes to air, causes green house effect and gets dissolved in water. What will be the effect on soil fertility and $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the water?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Vsv3a",
      "text": "Increases",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dkDKx",
      "text": "Decreases",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eFxB8",
      "text": "Remain same",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2UdMz",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$\r\nHere $\\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right]$ increases hence, $\\mathrm{pH}$ decreases due to which soil fertility will also decreases.",
